    description: "Christopher Langan is an American autodidact who has been described as having the highest IQ of any living American, with estimates ranging from 195 to 210 on extended-range tests. Raised in poverty across several US states, Langan taught himself advanced mathematics, philosophy, and physics largely without formal instruction, dropping out of college when he could not arrange transportation to class — a stark illustration of how circumstances can derail exceptional intelligence. He developed the Cognitive-Theoretic Model of the Universe (CTMU), a self-described 'theory of everything' that attempts to ground reality in a self-referential logical structure. His story is a central case study in Malcolm Gladwell's Outliers, examining how genius alone is insufficient without social capital and institutional support.",
