    iqContext: "Andreessen's estimated IQ of 152 reflects high giftedness in technical and strategic domains, with a particular strength in pattern recognition across technology cycles. His essay 'Software Is Eating the World' (2011) articulated a thesis — that every industry would eventually be transformed by software companies — that has proven remarkably prescient and has become a touchstone of technology investment strategy. His subsequent intellectual output through his blog and podcast has been distinctive for its willingness to stake clear, controversial positions on technology, economics, and politics. His 2023 'Techno-Optimist Manifesto' provoked intense debate for its full-throated embrace of technological acceleration as humanity's primary moral imperative — reflecting an unusually systematized ideological framework for a venture capitalist.",
